## Build, test, and verify

Never hard-code stack commands in skills, CI, or your own reasoning. Invoke **tasks**;
the {{ task_runner }} file is the single place real commands live.

{% if task_runner == "just" -%}
```bash
just lint        # static lint
just typecheck   # type / static analysis
just test        # unit tests
just build       # production build
just verify      # lint + typecheck + test (the pre-commit gate)
```
{%- elif task_runner == "make" -%}
```bash
make lint
make typecheck
make test
make build
make verify      # lint + typecheck + test (the pre-commit gate)
```
{%- elif task_runner == "npm" -%}
```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run test
npm run build
npm run verify   # lint + typecheck + test (the pre-commit gate)
```
{%- else -%}
This project declares no task runner. Define the commands for lint, typecheck, test,
and build in your README and keep them consistent — skills reference them by role,
not by literal command.
{%- endif %}

All three checks (lint, typecheck, test) must pass before any commit — this mirrors CI.

