## How to work here

| Situation | Flow |
| --- | --- |
| A freshly scaffolded, unconfigured harness | the **fg-bootstrap** skill — interview → stack ADRs + a wired task runner |
| A focused change (1 PR, a handful of files) | the **fg-plan** skill — it grills you before touching code |
{% if include_sdd -%}
| A feature with real architectural decisions | the **SDD pipeline**: `spec → plan → tasks → implement` |
| Several generated tasks to run together | **fg-execute-tasks** (one integration PR) |
{% endif -%}
{% if include_pr_review_ai -%}
| Reviewing a pull request | the **fg-pr-review** skill |
{% endif -%}
| A recurring stack pattern worth enforcing | **fg-create-skill** — author a domain skill |
| A choice the user should own | the **fg-decision-making** skill — ask, don't assume |

Skills live in `.agents/skills/` (source of truth). After editing one, regenerate the
adapters:

{% if task_runner == "just" -%}
```bash
just sync-adapters
```
{%- else -%}
```bash
node tools/sync-adapters.mjs
```
{%- endif %}

`docs/` explains each flow in depth.

